lear beat, a rhythm bed of one or two bars, then a melody shape that fits. Draft in syllables or simple notation, then test by clapping and singing. Edit for too many leaps if pitching is hard.","A comment that only says it looks nice with no element named.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no artistic reason."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about compose?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample: Rhythm | ta ti-ti ta ta | Melody contour up-up-down-home on C D E C. Draft revised to reduce a leap.\n\nTRY FIRST\nCreate a two-bar rhythm and describe a four-note melody contour that fits it.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: Rhythm written with ta/ti-ti; contour named with step/leap awareness.","explain":"Composing with rhythm and melody starts with a clear beat, a rhythm bed of one or two bars, then a melody shape that fits. Draft in syllables or simple notation, then test by clapping and singing. Edit for too many leaps if pitching is hard.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make intentional visual, music, drama or dance choices and name their effect, rather than saying an artwork is simply “nice”. Keep every claim linked to an element or technique.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the elements, techniques or performance choices that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. For movement or instruments, use a clear space, ask an adult to be nearby and stop if anything feels unsafe. You may always describe a choice instead of performing it. One deliberate artistic choice with a named effect is more useful than a longer praise sentence.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing pitches with no rhythm. Both layers need planning. Name the element or technique and its effect, not just decoration.","title":"Understand and demonstrate","visual":[{"alt":"Compose order.","caption":"Rhythm then tune.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.or